---
source: crates/cache-explorer-core/tests/golden.rs
description: "The same accesses with 12-bit addresses: three hex digits and a five-bit tag."
---
1.1 | decode | lineSize | - | - | Load 0x0A8: tag 0x01, set 2, offset 8 (word 2).
1.2 | miss | associativity | accesses, loads, misses, compulsory | - | Set 2 is invalid. Miss.
1.3 | victim | associativity | - | - | Set 2 has one way; the line goes there.
1.4 | fill | lineSize | valid 2/0, tag 2/0, word 2/0/0, word 2/0/1, word 2/0/2, word 2/0/3, fills | - | Fill way 0 with line 0x0A0–0x0AF from memory.
1.5 | complete | - | r1 | - | Read word 2 of way 0 (66) into r1.
2.1 | decode | lineSize | - | - | Load 0x028: tag 0x00, set 2, offset 8 (word 2).
2.2 | miss | associativity | accesses, loads, misses, compulsory | - | Set 2 holds tag 0x01, not 0x00. Miss.
2.3 | victim | associativity | - | - | Direct-mapped: way 0 is the only place for this line, so its current line must go.
2.4 | evict | associativity | valid 2/0, tag 2/0, word 2/0/0, word 2/0/1, word 2/0/2, word 2/0/3, evictions | - | Evict line 0x0A0 (tag 0x01) from way 0.
2.5 | fill | lineSize | valid 2/0, tag 2/0, word 2/0/0, word 2/0/1, word 2/0/2, word 2/0/3, fills | - | Fill way 0 with line 0x020–0x02F from memory.
2.6 | complete | - | r1 | - | Read word 2 of way 0 (38) into r1.
3.1 | decode | lineSize | - | - | Store 0x0A8: tag 0x01, set 2, offset 8 (word 2).
3.2 | miss | associativity | accesses, stores, misses, conflict | - | Set 2 holds tag 0x00, not 0x01. Miss.
3.3 | victim | associativity | - | - | Direct-mapped: way 0 is the only place for this line, so its current line must go.
3.4 | evict | associativity | valid 2/0, tag 2/0, word 2/0/0, word 2/0/1, word 2/0/2, word 2/0/3, evictions | - | Evict line 0x020 (tag 0x00) from way 0.
3.5 | fill | lineSize | valid 2/0, tag 2/0, word 2/0/0, word 2/0/1, word 2/0/2, word 2/0/3, fills | - | Fill way 0 with line 0x0A0–0x0AF from memory.
3.6 | write | writePolicy | dirty 2/0, word 2/0/2 | - | Write 7 into word 2 of way 0 and set its dirty bit. Memory at 0x0A8 is now stale.
